{ In this study we'll review basic plans for less common answers to the classic Normal Variation. } 1. e4 { That's the King's Pawn Game, leading to Open or Semi-open openings. } { [%csl Ge4][%cal Ge4d5] } (1. d4 { Queen's Pawn Game leads to Closed openings. } { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gd4e5,Gd7d5] }) 1... e5 { Most of the time, Black will respond with e5, going for the Open opening family. } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Ge5d4] } 2. Nf3 { Then the King's Knight Opening is the most obvious follow-up. } { [%cal Gf3e5,Gf3d4] } 2... Nc6 { To which Black will most likely answer with the Normal Variation. This will allow the usual Italian, Spanish or Scotch openings. } { [%cal Gc6e5,Gc6d4] } *


