2... Nf6 { That's the Petrov's Defense. Instead of defending their pawn, Black decides to counter attack White’s pawn. } { [%cal Gf6e4] } 3. Nxe5 d6 { [%cal Gd6e5] } (3... Nc6 { No good way to defend our Knight, so better to exchange. } 4. Nxc6) (3... Nxe4 { We can attack the Knigth directly with the Queen. } 4. Qe2) 4. Nf3 Nxe4 5. d4 { Pawns have been traded, we continue with normal development taking the center. } { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gd4e5] } *


