1... e6 { That's the French Defense. Black wants to support the pawn push to d5 next move for stable anchor in the center. } { [%cal Gd7d5] } 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 { That's the Paulsen Variation. White develops a piece and defends the e4 pawn. } { [%cal Gc3e4] } 3... Nf6 { [%cal Gf6e4] } 4. e5 { That's the Steinitz Variation. White takes the center and gains a tempo on the Knight. } { [%cal Ge5f6] } 4... Nfd7 5. f4 { Gains a significant space advantage. } { [%cal Gf4e5] } *


